@startuml seq-delete-group
!include style.iuml
title Figure 8 (new): Delete a group with all its expenses and settlements — FR 1.7
actor Owner
participant ":GroupDetailActivity" as UI
participant ":ConfirmDialog" as CD
participant ":GroupViewModel" as VM
participant ":GroupRepository" as GR
participant "db : FirebaseFirestore\n(+ security rules)" as DB

Owner -> UI : menu → Delete group\n(only visible to the owner)
UI -> CD : show()
alt Owner taps Cancel
  CD --> UI : nothing happens
else Owner confirms
  CD -> VM : deleteGroup()
  VM -> VM : isOwner()? (re-checked before the write)
  VM -> GR : deleteGroup(groupId, cb)
  GR -> DB : get groups/{groupId}/transactions
  DB --> GR : documents
  loop batches of at most 450 writes
    GR -> DB : WriteBatch.delete(transaction ...); the last batch\nalso deletes groups/{groupId}; commit()
  end
  note right of DB #FFE7C2 : CHANGED rules: besides each transaction's creator,\nthe group owner may delete transactions, otherwise\na group holding other members' expenses could\nnever be deleted (FR 1.7 vs FR 2.7)
  DB --> GR : ok
  GR --> VM : cb.onSuccess(null)
  VM --> UI : groupDeleted (Event)
  UI --> Owner : "Group deleted", back to the group list
end
@enduml
